  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nAbout the only thing to look forward to in the long term is that the \nLREF and global models are all in agreement in slowly meandering the \nupper ridge west through the weekend, to the vicinity of the Four \nCorners.  This will decrease thicknesses a little, offering some \nrelief from highs the next couple of days as we approach KMAF's \nclimatological peak of temperatures for the year.  Additional Heat \nAdvisories may be warranted after Tuesday.  Toward the weekend, the \nridge may be far enough west that isolated convection may creep back \ninto the mix, mainly Southeast New Mexico and the higher terrain of \nWest Texas. But chances will be minimal at best.",
